From 073011402b1425165ab1e76fcc7e75450f9988da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicholas Smith <nsmith@tenstorrent.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:15:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [feat] Opt-in original prompt lengths on prefill

agentic-models patch P3 (vllm-tt-plugin-original-prompt-lens.patch).

A model declaring model_capabilities['supports_original_prompt_lens']=True gets
TTModelInput.original_prompt_lens captured on the front-packed and lane prefill
paths and passed as prefill_forward(original_prompt_lens=...) on every route.
Base: m3 215effd part 1 only (capture/forward). Part 2, the host prefill
penalty-history split, is not taken: it would change host sampling for every
model.

Undeclared, nothing is captured (the field stays None) and the prefill call is
the f6fe76b one. The declaration is validated as a boolean at platform init.
The lane decode TTModelInput construction keeps the default None.

Tests: tests/test_original_prompt_lens.py, the capture/forward cases of
215effd's test_prefill_penalty_history.py plus undeclared cases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
